# Every platform checks out the bytes that are committed. Golden files, corpora, vault and
# timecapsule fixtures and README.md (the sdist description) are compared byte for byte, and
# Windows' core.autocrlf would otherwise turn their LF into CRLF. Files committed with CRLF stay
# CRLF (git's text=auto leaves them alone); new text files are committed with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.parquet binary
*.arrow binary
*.zip binary
*.bin binary
*.shapevault binary

# Shipped value lists, the golden byte corpus and the time-capsule corpus are bytes, not text: a
# checkout must not change their line ends (docs/GENERATION_STABILITY.md, "Byte-identical files";
# the time capsule: lead decision 2026-10-06, W8-04b).
src/shape/builtins/strategies/pools/** -text
src/shape/builtins/strategies/locales/** -text
tests/generation/golden_bytes/** -text
tests/timecapsule/corpus/** -text
